  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Life Sciences and Health Fact-finding Mission Nigeria to the Netherlands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This fact-finding visit aims to strengthen the relationship between Nigeria and The Netherlands and enhance private sector and economic cooperation on the identified priority area of Dutch&#x2013;Nigerian economic collaboration, Life Science and Health in Lagos and Abuja. The visit to Life Sciences and Health can help achieve the following goals: &#x2022;	Consolidate on post-covid business opportunities as identified in the updated Healthcare market study report whilst strengthening the existing bilateral or economic cooperation, specifically in Life Sciences and Healthcare both at the national and regional level;&#x2022;	The Nigerian delegation will learn about the Dutch approach and solutions in the Life Science and Health sector and the Dutch governance model, also known as the Dutch diamond approach;&#x2022;	The Nigerian delegation will be introduced to relevant stakeholders in this sector. There will be a showcase of Dutch expertise, technology and best practices. There is ample opportunity for Dutch-Nigerian business cooperation;&#x2022;	Building strong Dutch-Nigerian networks, facilitating knowledge exchange and discussing the objectives under the Dutch-Nigerian Memorandum of Understanding (MoU), signed in 2018. The visit also contributes to implementing this MoU, aiming to foster economic cooperation, trade and investment. With Dutch expertise, technology and PSD support, Nigeria can further develop sectors and increase its profitability, creating jobs for the growing young population. This fact-finding mission also offers opportunities for the Dutch private sector in the largest African economy. This incoming Nigerian delegation to the NL is a building block for outgoing Dutch Delegations to Nigeria in 2023.</narrative>
  </description>
